Review Response Strategy: Responding at Scale
Responding to negative reviews isn’t difficult on a case-by-case basis—but at scale, it becomes more complex. Here’s a look at your best options:

Type of Negative review responses
For small businesses, human-led responses to negative reviews are often the strongest choice. When business leaders or a customer service rep personally engage with customers, they can deliver helpful, customized replies that make a real impact.

For medium to large businesses, scale becomes a challenge. Human-led responses are still possible, but outsourcing them often means sacrificing quality and personalization. Spelling and grammar errors are common, and outsourced responders typically lack the context needed to speak knowledgeably about your business.

Generic AI or templates are another route—but usually the least effective. They’re easy to spot and lack any meaningful personalization or useful information.

Generative AI or ChatGPT for Review Response
When you’re managing hundreds—or even thousands—of reviews, writing personalized replies by hand can be overwhelming. Generative AI offers a scalable solution, and there are two main ways to use it.

The cheapest way is to use ChatGPT or another AI chatbot. Paste in the review, ask it to write a response, then copy and paste the reply as your review response. Repeat as needed. But there’s a catch: generic AI won’t know much about your business, so the response will likely lack relevance. We wrote more about this in our article, ChatGPT for Review Responses.

